{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"DECISION 1 - FINANCIAL FIGURES IN THE EARLIER SESSION LOG: ANNOTATE, DO NOT REDACT. Executed. The Wave 1 arm-characterisation comment in log 4d1f-8149-f3b8-4790 states per-run unit costs as bare decimals. Reasoning, in order of weight. (a) Redaction does not unpublish: the branch auto-pushes to a public repository, so clones and remote object retention mean the figures are already out; a rewrite changes current state, not exposure. (b) No proportionate tool exists - rebar comments are append-only with no edit or redact verb, ticket delete would destroy the entire 26-comment Wave 1 and Wave 2 record to remove two parentheticals, and history rewrite runs through tracker-maintenance --force, a human-only break-glass that agents are prohibited from using. (c) The 96f3 precedent differs materially: those were spend totals on planning tickets removable as whole tickets, not two sub-dollar third-party unit costs embedded in the study's primary durable record. (d) The live residual risk is propagation into a published writeup, which an annotation addresses and a rewrite would not. Action taken: a policy-annotation comment was appended to the earlier log stating the policy, instructing later readers and agents not to carry the figures into any writeup, pointing at the local-only reports, and recording that the choice was deliberate rather than an oversight. Escalation path if the owner disagrees: the removal is a human operator action via tracker-maintenance --force with a stated reason, and it should be weighed against destroying or rewriting the primary Wave 1 and 2 record."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789449249587579001,"uuid":"1b312008-4479-42d8-abec-e6fab7b214ef"}